    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0854" n="744" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg744"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">791.003/151: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Persia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-17T11:00:00+03:25"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 12:45
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>73. Department’s mail instruction No. 621 of May 31.<anchor n="59"
                        xml:id="d640-f1"/> The treaty section of the Persian Foreign Office objects
                    to the refusal of the consulate at Teheran to issue a nonimmigrant treaty-alien
                    visa and claims a contravention of the favored-nation stipulation in paragraph 2
                    of the provisional arrangement dated May 14 between Persia and the United
                        States.<anchor n="60" xml:id="d640-f2"/> Unless the principle involved is
                    clarified satisfactorily, difficulties may be encountered in regard to other
                    provisions of that agreement. Has the Department any further instructions?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
